1
00:00:01,101 --> 00:00:03,195
<i>- Previously on</i> Gotham...
- It's a miracle.

2
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:05,463
- How do you feel?
- Different.

3
00:00:05,606 --> 00:00:08,235
- His name is Will Thomas.
- Detective Gordon?

4
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:10,139
My friends... you'll save them.

5
00:00:10,277 --> 00:00:12,473
Say hello to Butch.

6
00:00:14,248 --> 00:00:16,046
BARBARA (echoing): <i>No!</i>

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,512
Gordon comes with me.

8
00:00:19,152 --> 00:00:21,644
I'll take his head, and you
can have the rest of him.

9
00:00:28,462 --> 00:00:29,672
This what got you
all hot and bothered?

10
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:30,696
Crazy bi...

11
00:00:32,099 --> 00:00:33,260
Not all square yet, though.

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,665
You're gonna help me do
what we all know needs doing.

13
00:00:35,802 --> 00:00:38,033
- What's that?
- Kill Penguin.

14
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:39,382
- You made it.
- Show me what you got.

15
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:40,738
LUCIUS: 250 apartments.

16
00:00:41,074 --> 00:00:43,339
Once the kids we've liberated
moved in, word got out

17
00:00:43,477 --> 00:00:45,837
pretty fast that there was a
safe place to live in the city.

18
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:48,139
(grunts) You wanted to know
where the Street Demonz

19
00:00:48,282 --> 00:00:49,282
base was.

20
00:00:51,451 --> 00:00:52,248
Where is everybody?

21
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:53,820
Holy crap.

22
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:57,623
What about that?

23
00:00:59,526 --> 00:01:00,755
Penguin did this.

24
00:01:03,664 --> 00:01:07,431
CHOIR: ♪ Oh, Penguin ♪

25
00:01:07,568 --> 00:01:09,730
♪ Our hero ♪

26
00:01:10,337 --> 00:01:12,533
♪ He knows ♪

27
00:01:12,673 --> 00:01:15,268
♪ No fear-o ♪

28
00:01:15,809 --> 00:01:18,074
♪ He brings us joy ♪

29
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:20,544
♪ And cheer-o ♪

30
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:23,376
♪ Oh, Penguin ♪

31
00:01:23,517 --> 00:01:25,418
♪ Our king ♪

32
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,415
♪ Oh, Penguin ♪

33
00:01:28,555 --> 00:01:31,081
♪ Our Penguin ♪

34
00:01:31,224 --> 00:01:33,557
♪ He's brave and clever ♪

35
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:36,163
♪ And kind ♪

36
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:37,654
♪ With a strong ♪

37
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:41,565
♪ Resourceful mind ♪

38
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:46,263
♪ He rules our land all day ♪

39
00:01:46,807 --> 00:01:51,711
♪ In the most magnificent way ♪

40
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:54,111
♪ Oh, Penguin ♪

41
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:57,443
♪ Oh, Penguin, oh, Penguin ♪

42
00:01:57,584 --> 00:02:00,213
♪ Our king, oh,
Penguin, our king ♪

43
00:02:00,354 --> 00:02:01,481
♪ Oh, Penguin... ♪

44
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:04,456
Production is
steady, Mr. Cobblepot.

45
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:07,150
Our stores contain 512

46
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:09,763
loaves of bread, 2,001 liters

47
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:10,761
of filtered water,

48
00:02:10,897 --> 00:02:13,366
400,232 bullets,

49
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,731
- (moans)
- and...

50
00:02:15,869 --> 00:02:18,737
(singing sputters, stops)

51
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,742
Penn, why is my
countertenor out cold?

52
00:02:23,176 --> 00:02:24,804
I-I'm sorry, Mr. Cobblepot.

53
00:02:25,345 --> 00:02:28,543
Uh... everyone was
working through the night

54
00:02:28,682 --> 00:02:29,741
in the bullet factory.

55
00:02:30,217 --> 00:02:32,243
We've been, uh, shorthanded,

56
00:02:32,753 --> 00:02:34,381
since people started defecting.

57
00:02:34,688 --> 00:02:35,688
Defecting?

58
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:37,723
You've been holding
out on me, Penn.

59
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:39,884
A thousand apologies.
I-I simply couldn't stand

60
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:41,738
seeing you upset while
you were recovering.

61
00:02:41,762 --> 00:02:44,755
Just tell me
everything! (exclaims)

62
00:02:44,898 --> 00:02:47,663
Rumor is they've fled to a place

63
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:49,402
called Haven,

64
00:02:49,536 --> 00:02:52,199
in Jim Gordon's sector.

65
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:55,503
My subjects are
fleeing to Jim Gordon?

66
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,872
After he shot me?!

67
00:02:58,211 --> 00:02:59,736
What about the bounty
on Gordon's head?

68
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,781
We've had trouble
finding takers.

69
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:03,383
The gangs are too disorganized,

70
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:05,384
and-and ordinary people, well...

71
00:03:06,586 --> 00:03:07,815
they love him, sir.

72
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:12,624
They should love me.

73
00:03:13,493 --> 00:03:14,222
Without me,

74
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:16,830
this entire island
would sink into chaos!

75
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:19,489
It's not just us.

76
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,927
People from every territory
are fleeing to Haven.

77
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:25,563
(laughs) Finally. Breakfast.

78
00:03:26,973 --> 00:03:28,771
(grunting)

79
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:32,378
(whimpers)

80
00:03:42,456 --> 00:03:43,456
Ha!

81
00:03:43,657 --> 00:03:45,751
The Street Demonz! (chuckles)

82
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,520
To what do I owe this honor?

83
00:03:47,661 --> 00:03:49,596
You hit our stronghold
and killed our men.

84
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:52,666
Not just us. You hit the Lo
Boyz and the Undead, too.

85
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:53,831
Did I, now?

86
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:55,697
You tagged the
scenes with graffiti

87
00:03:55,836 --> 00:03:57,566
that said "Penguin was here."

88
00:03:57,704 --> 00:03:58,899
You dolt.

89
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,970
If I wanted to start a gang war,

90
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:03,401
you'd all be dead.

91
00:04:03,543 --> 00:04:06,012
I wouldn't leave a
few and sign my name.

92
00:04:06,346 --> 00:04:07,746
Someone wanted you to attack me.

93
00:04:09,282 --> 00:04:11,012
- That's a good point.
- Mm-hmm.

94
00:04:11,485 --> 00:04:12,885
We didn't really
think this through.

95
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:16,822
No. Well, there will be
plenty of time for thinking

96
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:20,017
when my men are
ripping out your fingernails.

97
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,419
Chain him up.

98
00:04:21,561 --> 00:04:23,029
Wait! No!

99
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:24,530
Tighten our borders.

100
00:04:24,731 --> 00:04:28,327
No one in or out,
or it's your head.

101
00:04:28,535 --> 00:04:29,535
(chuckles)

102
00:04:31,671 --> 00:04:32,671
(dog whines)

103
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:36,532
That's right, Edward.

104
00:04:36,676 --> 00:04:38,577
It's Mr. Penn's head!

105
00:04:39,513 --> 00:04:42,813
It's his head! You're a
good dog, aren't you?

106
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,444
(grunts)

107
00:05:09,075 --> 00:05:10,373
(coughs)

108
00:05:27,527 --> 00:05:29,428
♪♪

109
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,578
♪♪

110
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,428
BULLOCK: <i>Word of
this place is spreading</i>

111
00:05:52,452 --> 00:05:54,512
like a bad case of the
clap. We got refugees

112
00:05:54,654 --> 00:05:56,520
coming in from every
territory in Gotham.

113
00:05:56,656 --> 00:05:58,818
Can you blame 'em? You
saw what it was like out there.

114
00:05:59,459 --> 00:06:01,360
People being
starved and terrorized,

115
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:03,122
used by the gangs
as slave labor.

116
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:05,728
You think those same gangs
aren't gonna want 'em back?

117
00:06:05,999 --> 00:06:08,434
Sooner or later, they're
gonna come looking for us.

118
00:06:09,669 --> 00:06:10,669
Let 'em.

119
00:06:10,737 --> 00:06:12,467
Hey, I get it,

120
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:15,809
but after our excursion
through nightmareville last week,

121
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:18,602
we hardly have any
ammo left... sorry...

122
00:06:18,745 --> 00:06:20,145
And we barely have any food.

123
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,778
Okay, all right.

124
00:06:21,948 --> 00:06:23,644
This is the only safe
place left in Gotham.

125
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:24,870
I'm not turning people away.

126
00:06:24,985 --> 00:06:26,886
I was afraid you
were gonna say that.

127
00:06:27,487 --> 00:06:29,547
- Hey, how you feeling? How, is uh...
- I'm fine.

128
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:31,819
You getting any sleep?

129
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:35,588
You've been going
full tilt for months.

130
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,758
Carrying the weight of everyone.

131
00:06:37,931 --> 00:06:40,400
Share the load. We
can't have you fall apart.

132
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,133
Thanks. I'm okay.

133
00:06:51,478 --> 00:06:53,071
Please tell me some good news.

134
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,473
Water purification
system repurposed

135
00:06:55,615 --> 00:06:57,174
from Wayne Enterprises tech.

136
00:06:59,152 --> 00:07:01,553
I know it's a drop in the
bucket, but every bit helps.

137
00:07:01,721 --> 00:07:03,833
That's the last can of beans!
I ain't had my rations yet!

138
00:07:03,857 --> 00:07:04,400
Think I have?

139
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,040
- (chatter continues)
- Hey, break it up.

140
00:07:06,064 --> 00:07:07,064
Break it up! Break it up.

141
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,600
For all the new people here...

142
00:07:17,671 --> 00:07:20,106
everyone is welcome in
Haven, but there are rules.

143
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:23,573
And one of them is we
leave the fighting outside.

144
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:28,808
Government already
thinks we don't deserve help.

145
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:31,718
We have to show otherwise.

146
00:07:34,988 --> 00:07:36,854
Gangs want to tear
themselves apart outside,

147
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,014
that's their business.

148
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,990
In here, in Haven...

149
00:07:42,896 --> 00:07:44,694
we help each other survive.

150
00:07:55,608 --> 00:07:56,940
Your speech worked.

151
00:07:57,577 --> 00:07:58,738
For now.

152
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:01,740
What happens when they find out
the government abandoned them?

153
00:08:03,216 --> 00:08:04,216
Sorry.

154
00:08:04,584 --> 00:08:05,584
For what?

155
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:08,313
Jim, you're holding
this place together.

156
00:08:08,755 --> 00:08:10,485
You're giving these people hope.

157
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:12,586
Hope can only go so far.

158
00:08:13,526 --> 00:08:14,726
Not to put more on your plate,

159
00:08:14,794 --> 00:08:17,889
but the kid whose friends
you saved from the slavers...

160
00:08:18,231 --> 00:08:20,132
His bunkmates say he's
been having nightmares.

161
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,001
Last night he fell off his bed
half-asleep, broke his arm.

162
00:08:23,136 --> 00:08:24,695
Maybe you could talk to him.

163
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,505
(mouths)

164
00:08:30,043 --> 00:08:31,043
Hey.

165
00:08:34,914 --> 00:08:36,594
You don't feel like
joining the other kids?

166
00:08:39,119 --> 00:08:41,679
We can't even begin to imagine
what you've been through.

167
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:45,084
But it's over. You're safe now.

168
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:49,292
I promise I will never let
anyone hurt you ever again.

169
00:08:50,764 --> 00:08:51,764
Okay?

170
00:08:54,234 --> 00:08:55,862
I got something for you.

171
00:08:58,772 --> 00:08:59,933
From my rations.

172
00:09:00,273 --> 00:09:01,832
Little pineapple.

173
00:09:04,811 --> 00:09:06,109
Hang in there.

174
00:09:08,648 --> 00:09:10,776
I'll come check
on you later, okay?

175
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:14,148
(Gordon sighs)

176
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,618
(indistinct conversations)

177
00:09:25,298 --> 00:09:26,095
Selina?

178
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:27,232
One second.

179
00:09:27,934 --> 00:09:28,697
What are you doing out of bed?

180
00:09:28,835 --> 00:09:30,035
The doctor said you need rest.

181
00:09:30,804 --> 00:09:32,705
Does it look like I need rest?

182
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,765
No, but...

183
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:39,209
Look, whatever
Ivy's root did to me...

184
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:41,843
I've never felt better.

185
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:45,684
So now I have to find
the freak who shot me.

186
00:09:47,654 --> 00:09:49,265
I've been looking for Jeremiah
since the bridges blew.

187
00:09:49,289 --> 00:09:50,621
I haven't found a thing.

188
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:52,654
Right, but there have
never been refugees

189
00:09:52,792 --> 00:09:54,624
in the Green Zone before.

190
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:58,731
These people come from
all over Gotham, Bruce.

191
00:09:58,865 --> 00:10:01,334
Someone has to know something.

192
00:10:02,168 --> 00:10:05,138
I want to find Jeremiah
just as much as you do.

193
00:10:06,139 --> 00:10:08,499
But even if we find him, he's
had months to fortify himself.

194
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:09,735
We can't go after him alone.

195
00:10:10,076 --> 00:10:11,169
You scared, Bruce?

196
00:10:11,644 --> 00:10:13,010
(quietly): Of course I'm scared.

197
00:10:14,714 --> 00:10:16,239
Jeremiah shot you to get to me.

198
00:10:16,382 --> 00:10:17,748
He almost killed you.

199
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:19,118
I won't lose you.

200
00:10:20,086 --> 00:10:21,816
I'm not yours to lose.

201
00:10:24,057 --> 00:10:28,085
You can't stop me from
going after Jeremiah.

202
00:10:29,662 --> 00:10:31,688
But I am asking you for help.

203
00:10:33,066 --> 00:10:34,762
We take him
down, we do it right.

204
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:36,135
We bring him back here,

205
00:10:36,269 --> 00:10:38,898
and he stands trial for turning
Gotham into a madhouse.

206
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:41,866
(chuckles softly)

207
00:10:42,008 --> 00:10:43,008
What?

208
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:54,788
I was hoping I
could count on you.

209
00:10:57,090 --> 00:11:00,891
I heard rumors about
Jeremiah in the Dark Zone,

210
00:11:01,094 --> 00:11:03,325
but who knows if they're true.

211
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:05,154
SELINA: The Dark Zone?

212
00:11:05,265 --> 00:11:06,756
On the other end of the island.

213
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:08,360
It's chaos,

214
00:11:09,936 --> 00:11:12,701
ruled by those
who've lost their minds

215
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:15,001
since the bridges went down.

216
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:23,308
They said Jeremiah is
there, gathering followers.

217
00:11:24,083 --> 00:11:25,176
Sounds like a lead.

218
00:11:25,718 --> 00:11:27,812
No. You can't go there.

219
00:11:27,954 --> 00:11:28,978
You'll die.

220
00:11:29,255 --> 00:11:30,814
We fought Jeremiah before.

221
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:33,025
You don't understand.

222
00:11:33,393 --> 00:11:34,691
If you go to the Dark Zone,

223
00:11:34,827 --> 00:11:37,387
Jeremiah is the
least of your worries.

224
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:40,124
Everyone there is insane.

225
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:44,303
Look at what they
did to my friend.

226
00:11:54,847 --> 00:11:58,784
- Penn, where the...?!
- OLGA: ♪ Penguin, my hero ♪

227
00:11:58,985 --> 00:12:02,217
♪ He having no fear-o... ♪

228
00:12:02,355 --> 00:12:03,084
Stop.

229
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:06,284
- ♪ He bringing joy
and cheer-o. ♪
- Stop!

230
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:08,093
Where is my staff?

231
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:09,127
Where is Mr. Penn?

232
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:12,730
Um, they're having to, um...

233
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:16,064
defected to Haven.

234
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:19,339
And my guards didn't stop them?

235
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:22,908
My guards, too?

236
00:12:25,378 --> 00:12:26,378
Edward?

237
00:12:28,314 --> 00:12:30,146
Edward! Edward!

238
00:12:33,086 --> 00:12:34,748
They took my dog?

239
00:12:35,221 --> 00:12:38,988
Rumors say pup went willingly.

240
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:42,452
Lies!

241
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:49,827
You're in luck, my friend.

242
00:12:50,003 --> 00:12:53,098
Jim Gordon is luring people
from every territory in Gotham

243
00:12:53,306 --> 00:12:54,535
including yours.

244
00:12:55,008 --> 00:12:57,307
As our interests
are now aligned,

245
00:12:57,910 --> 00:13:01,039
I have decided
that you may live.

246
00:13:06,886 --> 00:13:08,821
He's been dead since yesterday.

247
00:13:09,989 --> 00:13:12,823
Contact the Lo Boyz
and the Undead.

248
00:13:13,192 --> 00:13:15,957
You have men, vehicles and gas.

249
00:13:16,162 --> 00:13:17,528
I have the bullets.

250
00:13:18,431 --> 00:13:21,924
It's time we paid a
visit to this Haven...

251
00:13:23,436 --> 00:13:24,961
right after I put
on some clothes.

252
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:32,309
Jim! Border guards just radioed.

253
00:13:33,012 --> 00:13:34,423
Penguin broke
through the barricades.

254
00:13:34,447 --> 00:13:36,125
Street Demonz, other
gangs rolling with him.

255
00:13:36,149 --> 00:13:37,515
They're heading for Haven.

256
00:13:38,084 --> 00:13:40,462
- We can beat them there. Load up!
- What the hell are we gonna do?

257
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:43,422
- We don't have more than a
dozen bullets between us.
- You're right.

258
00:13:44,223 --> 00:13:45,334
We get in a firefight
and we're dead.

259
00:13:45,358 --> 00:13:47,589
Okay, I'm gonna need
you to go get some help.

260
00:13:47,994 --> 00:13:49,519
I'm not sure we
got any friends left.

261
00:13:50,363 --> 00:13:51,956
I'm hoping we still have one.

262
00:13:52,465 --> 00:13:54,491
(dog barking)

263
00:13:59,439 --> 00:14:01,465
So, this is the Dark Zone.

264
00:14:03,276 --> 00:14:04,904
They should call
it the Dull Zone.

265
00:14:05,611 --> 00:14:07,011
Place is dead.

266
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,180
(chuckles) What?

267
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:12,050
You seem yourself again.

268
00:14:13,286 --> 00:14:14,286
I'm glad.

269
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,320
Wait, I know this block.

270
00:14:19,592 --> 00:14:21,561
Used to be the
posh part of town.

271
00:14:22,895 --> 00:14:24,625
Everyone with money got out.

272
00:14:25,398 --> 00:14:26,422
You didn't.

273
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:30,031
I had a reason to stay.

274
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:40,035
MAN: Oh, God!

275
00:14:40,313 --> 00:14:41,941
Help me, please.

276
00:14:42,482 --> 00:14:43,642
- Wait. Wait, wait.
- Come on.

277
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,174
Oh, God.

278
00:14:45,318 --> 00:14:46,342
Get down.

279
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:56,425
(people cackling)

280
00:14:59,499 --> 00:15:02,298
Now we know who carved
"kill" into that guy's chest.

281
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:06,433
Do you think they know
anything about Jeremiah?

282
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:09,041
Let's find someone else to ask.

283
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:12,443
Let's go before they see us.

284
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:19,584
(chuckles)

285
00:15:19,952 --> 00:15:20,952
Kill!

286
00:15:21,554 --> 00:15:22,954
We're not here for you.

287
00:15:23,956 --> 00:15:25,686
We're looking for
Jeremiah Valeska.

288
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:29,061
Kill you. Kill Jeremiah.

289
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:32,289
I don't think this guy is
much of a talker, Bruce.

290
00:15:35,134 --> 00:15:36,227
What do you want to do?

291
00:15:36,469 --> 00:15:37,469
Easy.

292
00:15:40,006 --> 00:15:42,100
Find the schoolyard's
biggest bully...

293
00:15:44,510 --> 00:15:46,172
- (shouts)
- and kick his teeth in.

294
00:15:50,349 --> 00:15:52,011
(grunts) The
chicky-chick is mine.

295
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:01,660
Selina.

296
00:16:09,502 --> 00:16:11,368
♪ Mine eyes have
seen the glory ♪

297
00:16:11,504 --> 00:16:13,473
♪ Of the coming of the Lord ♪

298
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,699
♪ He is trampling
out the vintage ♪

299
00:16:16,042 --> 00:16:17,722
♪ Where the grapes
of wrath are stored... ♪

300
00:16:19,245 --> 00:16:21,544
Everyone inside. Inside.

301
00:16:23,449 --> 00:16:24,678
Let's go. Get inside.

302
00:16:25,351 --> 00:16:26,444
(screams)

303
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:28,052
What's going on, Captain Gordon?

304
00:16:28,554 --> 00:16:29,554
Inside, go.

305
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:34,589
Hold your fire.

306
00:16:40,233 --> 00:16:41,724
Hold your fire.

307
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:58,181
Well, if it isn't my
old friend Mr. Penn

308
00:16:59,285 --> 00:17:02,312
and the Gertrud
Kapelput Memorial Choir.

309
00:17:02,455 --> 00:17:07,359
Oh, it is so nice to see
some familiar faces!

310
00:17:07,493 --> 00:17:09,155
You shouldn't have
come here, Oswald.

311
00:17:09,295 --> 00:17:13,528
Oh, well, perhaps you shouldn't
have stolen my people or my dog.

312
00:17:13,799 --> 00:17:16,325
Every refugee is here
of their own free will

313
00:17:16,469 --> 00:17:18,335
and under the
protection of the GCPD.

314
00:17:18,471 --> 00:17:19,700
Edward!

315
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,039
Edward!

316
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,168
Come here!

317
00:17:24,644 --> 00:17:25,805
Right now!

318
00:17:27,246 --> 00:17:28,566
I will make this
very simple, Jim.

319
00:17:29,115 --> 00:17:34,144
You return our people
and Edward and an apology

320
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:37,185
or we will destroy this
little commune of yours

321
00:17:37,323 --> 00:17:39,554
and salt the earth
on which it stands.

322
00:17:39,692 --> 00:17:40,523
The answer is no.

323
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,561
Now turn around unless
you want a bloodbath.

324
00:17:42,695 --> 00:17:44,425
Let me explain something, Jim.

325
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:46,463
I heard about
your little excursion

326
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:47,828
through the territories.

327
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:51,103
So, whatever ammo
you stole from me,

328
00:17:51,437 --> 00:17:54,100
I'm betting you used it up,

329
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,766
which means you're bluffing.

330
00:18:07,853 --> 00:18:09,651
You want to test us, Oswald?

331
00:18:11,624 --> 00:18:13,752
I'm sure my men could
use the target practice.

332
00:18:15,294 --> 00:18:16,694
Slice and dice, little chicky.

333
00:18:16,829 --> 00:18:17,829
You look soft.

334
00:18:18,164 --> 00:18:19,757
You look like 300
pounds of ugly.

335
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:22,125
(laughs) Kill and kill.

336
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:27,665
Where's Jeremiah?

337
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:42,486
(shouts)

338
00:18:46,325 --> 00:18:46,883
Where is Jeremiah?

339
00:18:47,226 --> 00:18:48,226
Jeremiah?

340
00:18:48,894 --> 00:18:50,453
(groans)

341
00:18:53,232 --> 00:18:55,895
Tell me where
Jeremiah is or my face

342
00:18:56,369 --> 00:18:59,897
is going to be the
last thing you ever see.

343
00:19:00,239 --> 00:19:01,764
Old Town North, okay?

344
00:19:02,174 --> 00:19:03,267
We don't mess with him.

345
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,134
Old Town North?

346
00:19:05,745 --> 00:19:07,304
You wouldn't lie
to me, would you?

347
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,841
It's the truth.

348
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:15,682
Selina, he's had enough.

349
00:19:15,921 --> 00:19:16,786
He's had enough

350
00:19:16,922 --> 00:19:19,448
when I say he's had enough.

351
00:19:25,297 --> 00:19:27,323
(Selina grunts)

352
00:19:28,601 --> 00:19:30,160
What the hell?

353
00:19:32,938 --> 00:19:34,270
You won.

354
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,169
It's over.

355
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,709
SELINA: Old Town North. See?

356
00:19:40,579 --> 00:19:42,343
That was easy.

357
00:19:44,417 --> 00:19:45,715
What are we waiting for?

358
00:19:51,490 --> 00:19:52,834
You said they'll
be out of bullets.

359
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:54,292
He's bluffing, you idiot.

360
00:19:54,427 --> 00:19:55,427
How do you know?

361
00:19:55,961 --> 00:19:57,554
I know Jim Gordon.

362
00:19:58,397 --> 00:20:00,696
But if you require
a demonstration,

363
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:02,932
three of you, march.

364
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:04,928
But, uh, they have guns.

365
00:20:06,238 --> 00:20:08,571
(chuckles) So do I

366
00:20:09,475 --> 00:20:11,273
and mine is most
certainly loaded.

367
00:20:15,281 --> 00:20:16,305
On my mark.

368
00:20:19,685 --> 00:20:20,709
Make them count.

369
00:20:23,622 --> 00:20:25,557
(gun clicking)

370
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:34,358
OSWALD: Ah.

371
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,893
Well, Jim,

372
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:38,796
it seems you are
out of ammo, after all.

373
00:20:39,839 --> 00:20:41,808
Now, if you don't want your men

374
00:20:41,941 --> 00:20:44,410
to die in a hail of bullets,
you know what to do.

375
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:51,577
Fine. On the count of three.

376
00:20:51,717 --> 00:20:53,481
- One, two...
- All right.

377
00:20:53,786 --> 00:20:55,652
All right. Put them down.

378
00:20:57,757 --> 00:20:58,850
Put them down.

379
00:21:16,842 --> 00:21:18,606
Selina, what was
that back there?

380
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,276
They had to know I was serious.

381
00:21:22,414 --> 00:21:23,859
You didn't have
to hurt him like that.

382
00:21:23,883 --> 00:21:25,476
He was trying to kill me, Bruce,

383
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,015
just like Jeremiah
tried to kill me.

384
00:21:28,654 --> 00:21:30,520
So as far as I'm concerned...

385
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:34,021
he got off easy.

386
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:38,029
Whose side are you on, Bruce?

387
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:41,858
Yours. Always.

388
00:21:42,368 --> 00:21:44,360
Then let's do what
we came here to do.

389
00:21:49,408 --> 00:21:50,774
Looks like we're close.

390
00:22:07,593 --> 00:22:08,652
When I see him,

391
00:22:09,461 --> 00:22:11,054
I'm gonna tear his throat out.

392
00:22:11,964 --> 00:22:12,988
BRUCE: Selina.

393
00:22:29,481 --> 00:22:31,677
Welcome, pilgrims,

394
00:22:31,951 --> 00:22:34,546
to The Church of
Jeremiah Valeska.

395
00:22:34,987 --> 00:22:37,513
The only place where
you faithful pilgrims

396
00:22:37,656 --> 00:22:40,785
can become your
very best selves.

397
00:22:41,093 --> 00:22:42,652
(quietly): Who the hell is that?

398
00:22:43,395 --> 00:22:44,395
I don't know.

399
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:47,662
I bet she knows where
Jeremiah is, though.

400
00:22:48,534 --> 00:22:49,945
Stay here. I'm gonna
get a closer look.

401
00:22:49,969 --> 00:22:52,461
No. We do this together, Selina.

402
00:22:52,605 --> 00:22:53,605
That was the deal.

403
00:22:53,672 --> 00:22:55,470
Funny, I don't
remember saying that.

404
00:22:55,608 --> 00:22:59,067
Now, I know you've
come from far and wide

405
00:22:59,411 --> 00:23:00,970
to meet the man himself.

406
00:23:01,146 --> 00:23:05,948
But first, he requires
a show of faith.

407
00:23:06,685 --> 00:23:07,812
Don't be shy.

408
00:23:08,153 --> 00:23:10,452
Jeremiah awaits.

409
00:23:10,789 --> 00:23:12,485
Who is ready?

410
00:23:15,961 --> 00:23:17,759
(gasps) Lovely.

411
00:23:18,430 --> 00:23:21,127
Jeremiah will be so happy.

412
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:24,670
But remember: he wants only

413
00:23:24,803 --> 00:23:27,136
the most faithful followers.

414
00:23:28,107 --> 00:23:31,839
And you all have a
chance to prove yourself,

415
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:35,973
right up those stairs.

416
00:23:41,921 --> 00:23:44,914
And the rest of you, get out!

417
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,426
Selina.

418
00:23:50,195 --> 00:23:51,458
SELINA: Wait.

419
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:53,997
I want to meet Jeremiah.

420
00:23:54,166 --> 00:23:57,534
You don't look like one
of Jeremiah's worshipers.

421
00:23:57,836 --> 00:24:02,001
I have witnessed
his work firsthand.

422
00:24:02,908 --> 00:24:04,706
I will never forget it.

423
00:24:06,779 --> 00:24:08,714
Then right this way.

424
00:24:24,496 --> 00:24:25,555
(speaking indistinctly)

425
00:24:43,682 --> 00:24:44,682
You're gonna regret this.

426
00:24:44,717 --> 00:24:46,845
(laughs) Strong words,

427
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:48,648
for someone who
is out of options.

428
00:24:48,787 --> 00:24:50,255
(laughs)

429
00:24:50,589 --> 00:24:54,549
First, I'm gonna make you
watch while I destroy Haven.

430
00:24:56,762 --> 00:24:59,095
Then, I'm gonna shoot
you and leave you for dead,

431
00:24:59,231 --> 00:25:01,223
just like you did
to me. Sound fair?

432
00:25:01,567 --> 00:25:04,731
If the government liberates
the city and finds out about this,

433
00:25:04,870 --> 00:25:06,230
you'll be at the
top of their list.

434
00:25:06,672 --> 00:25:07,672
Wake up, Jim.

435
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:09,772
The government has abandoned us.

436
00:25:10,109 --> 00:25:14,672
The only law in Gotham is power,
and that power belongs to me.

437
00:25:15,647 --> 00:25:16,927
We have children here. Families.

438
00:25:17,049 --> 00:25:18,642
What happens when
the gangs take them?

439
00:25:18,784 --> 00:25:24,189
Hmm. They probably go
back to being slaves, I guess.

440
00:25:25,891 --> 00:25:27,189
My people, on the other hand,

441
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:29,256
will go back to
their regular lives,

442
00:25:29,661 --> 00:25:32,028
with their bellies full of
gruel and their heads full

443
00:25:32,164 --> 00:25:36,067
of wonderful thoughts about
their grand protector, me.

444
00:25:36,735 --> 00:25:39,728
If this is about revenge
against me, do your worst.

445
00:25:39,938 --> 00:25:41,304
But leave the
refugees out of it.

446
00:25:41,774 --> 00:25:42,935
So heroic.

447
00:25:43,976 --> 00:25:45,035
Almost tempting.

448
00:25:45,811 --> 00:25:48,542
But I think I'm gonna
stick to my original plan.

449
00:25:52,684 --> 00:25:54,846
Uh, Jim's gonna
die, isn't he, boy?

450
00:25:54,987 --> 00:25:56,580
Oh, you're a good
dog, yes, you are.

451
00:26:03,595 --> 00:26:04,595
Mr. Cobblepot.

452
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:07,064
Stop. That one belongs to me.

453
00:26:07,766 --> 00:26:11,294
No can do. You sacrificed one
of my guys calling the cop's bluff.

454
00:26:12,104 --> 00:26:13,231
So what?

455
00:26:14,273 --> 00:26:15,798
I said he's mine.

456
00:26:17,109 --> 00:26:19,340
Oh, thank you, Mr. Cobblepot.

457
00:26:21,980 --> 00:26:23,778
Then how about we
take your territory?

458
00:26:23,916 --> 00:26:25,043
And your bullet factory.

459
00:26:25,184 --> 00:26:27,085
Penn! Penn!

460
00:26:27,219 --> 00:26:29,085
(panting)

461
00:26:29,688 --> 00:26:31,953
I'm sorry, Mr. Cobblepot.

462
00:26:32,891 --> 00:26:34,325
You fool!

463
00:26:34,827 --> 00:26:36,955
This never would have
happened if you stayed with me.

464
00:26:37,096 --> 00:26:38,587
Why did you leave?

465
00:26:40,165 --> 00:26:42,293
Everyone hated you.

466
00:26:54,746 --> 00:26:58,114
You will pay for this!

467
00:26:58,984 --> 00:27:02,045
Hey, Penguin, you got
something on your face.

468
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:05,318
Let me go! We had a deal!

469
00:27:05,657 --> 00:27:06,989
Shut your mouth...

470
00:27:10,762 --> 00:27:14,824
or the next thing that comes
out your mouth is a bullet.

471
00:27:16,201 --> 00:27:17,829
Man, you are on fire!

472
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:24,066
I take it that didn't work
out the way you'd hoped.

473
00:27:29,047 --> 00:27:30,174
Barbara?

474
00:27:32,885 --> 00:27:33,944
Barbara?

475
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:36,019
Hey, you in here?

476
00:27:38,724 --> 00:27:39,384
You've gotten good at that.

477
00:27:39,725 --> 00:27:41,717
(chuckles) Haven't
you heard, Harvey?

478
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:43,419
No men in the
Sirens past midnight.

479
00:27:43,762 --> 00:27:46,107
Sorry to bust up ladies' night,
but Jim Gordon needs your help.

480
00:27:46,131 --> 00:27:50,865
Oh, perhaps it's time Golden
Boy learned to save himself.

481
00:27:51,303 --> 00:27:53,397
And aren't you tired
of playing sidekick?

482
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:55,402
See, I don't see it that way.

483
00:27:55,841 --> 00:27:56,934
Me and Jim are friends.

484
00:27:57,209 --> 00:27:58,973
We're fighting for
the same thing.

485
00:27:59,178 --> 00:28:00,298
It seemed like you got that.

486
00:28:00,379 --> 00:28:02,007
(chuckles)

487
00:28:02,381 --> 00:28:05,681
You know, I remember
when you first partnered up.

488
00:28:07,853 --> 00:28:10,015
He, the idealistic rookie.

489
00:28:10,822 --> 00:28:12,290
You, the cynical veteran.

490
00:28:12,457 --> 00:28:13,686
You were sane.

491
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:16,260
(laughs) Now you
carry his laundry.

492
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:18,373
Do you ever
wonder what your life

493
00:28:18,397 --> 00:28:22,164
might've been like if you'd
never met Jim Gordon?

494
00:28:22,301 --> 00:28:25,169
I'd be dead, or wishing I was.

495
00:28:26,004 --> 00:28:27,870
You're delusional, Harvey.

496
00:28:28,807 --> 00:28:31,470
Just like all the sad saps
who think the government

497
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:33,836
is just gonna sail
in and save them.

498
00:28:34,446 --> 00:28:37,245
Maybe. And look, I know you've
had your differences with Jim,

499
00:28:37,449 --> 00:28:39,179
but if you don't help him now,

500
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,358
- Penguin
and the other gangs...
- Penguin?

501
00:28:41,787 --> 00:28:43,085
You should've opened with that.

502
00:28:43,822 --> 00:28:44,915
Let's move!

503
00:28:47,859 --> 00:28:49,088
It's not working.

504
00:28:49,361 --> 00:28:51,091
We need to find a way
to cut these bindings.

505
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:52,721
Well, I'm not helping you, Jim.

506
00:28:53,265 --> 00:28:55,427
You are the reason
I'm in this predicament.

507
00:28:55,801 --> 00:28:57,429
You have taken
everything from me.

508
00:28:57,769 --> 00:28:58,930
Keep your voice down.

509
00:28:59,338 --> 00:29:02,331
I kept people safe. I
protected them from chaos.

510
00:29:02,474 --> 00:29:04,136
They should have loved <i>me.</i>

511
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:06,776
Instead, they came
here, to this pigsty,

512
00:29:06,912 --> 00:29:08,471
to be covered
in fleas and filth.

513
00:29:08,814 --> 00:29:10,874
Why? What makes
this place so special?

514
00:29:11,016 --> 00:29:13,212
Well, for one thing,
it's far away from you.

515
00:29:13,352 --> 00:29:16,015
Oh, that's rich, Jim.

516
00:29:16,154 --> 00:29:17,765
You should be proud
of yourself for that one.

517
00:29:17,789 --> 00:29:18,950
(whispers): Quiet.

518
00:29:23,495 --> 00:29:26,988
I think I saw someone
place a stash...

519
00:29:28,033 --> 00:29:29,262
there.

520
00:29:32,537 --> 00:29:34,301
- Who is that?
- A friend.

521
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,531
Just act normal.

522
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:38,001
I know it's a stretch.

523
00:29:47,219 --> 00:29:48,219
Hey.

524
00:29:50,989 --> 00:29:51,989
Bingo.

525
00:29:59,064 --> 00:30:00,965
(stifled laugh)

526
00:30:01,233 --> 00:30:02,410
I'm gonna get out of here, Jim.

527
00:30:02,434 --> 00:30:03,714
And I'm gonna
watch these animals

528
00:30:03,902 --> 00:30:05,268
tear this place to the ground.

529
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,630
So you make your way back
to your territory. Then what?

530
00:30:07,906 --> 00:30:09,183
Hmm? You don't
think that eventually,

531
00:30:09,207 --> 00:30:11,039
these gangs are
gonna come after you?

532
00:30:11,810 --> 00:30:13,142
We need to take them out.

533
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:15,075
Right here, right now.

534
00:30:23,055 --> 00:30:24,489
Now, how do we pick it up?

535
00:30:48,146 --> 00:30:49,146
(thuds)

536
00:31:14,239 --> 00:31:16,936
ECCO: I'll have to have a
word with the cleaning lady.

537
00:31:17,943 --> 00:31:21,004
Mind your step, pilgrims.

538
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:26,040
But first,

539
00:31:26,385 --> 00:31:28,183
the main attraction.

540
00:31:31,089 --> 00:31:32,455
Six-shooters.

541
00:31:33,925 --> 00:31:34,949
Bang, bang.

542
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:37,158
Each of you get one gun.

543
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,326
And one bullet.

544
00:31:42,334 --> 00:31:43,461
What is this?

545
00:31:43,969 --> 00:31:47,235
Like I said, a show of faith.

546
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:51,309
But if you're
ch-ch-ch-chicken...

547
00:32:02,254 --> 00:32:03,254
(gasps)

548
00:32:04,456 --> 00:32:05,583
Try me.

549
00:32:29,014 --> 00:32:32,507
Oh, my little pilgrims.

550
00:32:33,485 --> 00:32:37,445
This will make
Jeremiah so happy.

551
00:32:40,225 --> 00:32:41,420
Now,

552
00:32:41,993 --> 00:32:43,723
on the count of three.

553
00:32:45,163 --> 00:32:46,529
One...

554
00:32:49,067 --> 00:32:50,330
Two...

555
00:32:53,004 --> 00:32:54,004
Chicken poo.

556
00:32:57,476 --> 00:33:00,002
Just seeing if
y'all were listening.

557
00:33:04,182 --> 00:33:06,515
- Three!
- (gunshots)

558
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:13,315
ECCO: Well, well, well.

559
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:16,192
You disappoint me, curls.

560
00:33:17,295 --> 00:33:19,526
I had such high hopes for you.

561
00:33:20,732 --> 00:33:22,166
What, with that

562
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:25,466
cocky little swagger and all.

563
00:33:27,172 --> 00:33:28,697
I'm just not a mindless idiot

564
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:32,738
who's willing to get shot
in the head for nothing.

565
00:33:34,546 --> 00:33:35,741
Hear that?

566
00:33:36,615 --> 00:33:41,076
Curls is here to
judge all of us,

567
00:33:41,620 --> 00:33:45,489
to judge Jeremiah
and his methods.

568
00:33:46,658 --> 00:33:48,422
What a fitting reminder.

569
00:33:48,627 --> 00:33:50,095
To outsiders,

570
00:33:50,595 --> 00:33:54,032
Jeremiah's methods
may look like madness,

571
00:33:54,366 --> 00:33:56,232
but we believers know:

572
00:33:56,801 --> 00:34:01,296
his methods will
be our salvation.

573
00:34:01,573 --> 00:34:02,573
Now,

574
00:34:03,742 --> 00:34:06,302
I need to have a
word with our friend.

575
00:34:07,279 --> 00:34:08,577
The rest of you

576
00:34:09,247 --> 00:34:12,115
get straight A's.

577
00:34:12,384 --> 00:34:14,717
Please proceed

578
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:18,046
and be reborn.

579
00:34:22,594 --> 00:34:24,529
(humming)

580
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:44,447
- (blows landing)
- (men grunting)

581
00:34:50,488 --> 00:34:51,717
What's the matter?

582
00:34:52,390 --> 00:34:54,586
Don't you want to meet Jeremiah?

583
00:34:54,826 --> 00:34:55,826
I do.

584
00:34:56,795 --> 00:35:00,288
I'm just not willing to play
your little psychotic game.

585
00:35:00,632 --> 00:35:02,567
(laughs)

586
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:07,163
But, baby, it's so fun.

587
00:35:07,305 --> 00:35:08,773
If it's so fun,

588
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:11,266
why don't <i>you</i> play?

589
00:35:12,444 --> 00:35:13,878
Don't you get it?

590
00:35:14,846 --> 00:35:16,439
I have.

591
00:35:22,253 --> 00:35:23,778
The bullet's still inside.

592
00:35:24,589 --> 00:35:27,684
Rattling around this
old noggin of mine.

593
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:30,852
Ping. Ping.

594
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:32,389
Ping.

595
00:35:33,832 --> 00:35:37,269
Boy, do I feel it when
the nights get cold.

596
00:35:40,438 --> 00:35:41,438
(gun clicks)

597
00:35:42,841 --> 00:35:43,841
(gun clicks)

598
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:46,711
- (gun clicks)
- (laughing)

599
00:35:47,612 --> 00:35:48,841
You're insane.

600
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:51,839
No.

601
00:35:52,651 --> 00:35:56,144
I was willing to look
death in the face,

602
00:35:56,655 --> 00:35:59,625
to allow the old me to die.

603
00:36:00,392 --> 00:36:04,420
It's the gift Jeremiah's
brother Jerome gave him.

604
00:36:04,562 --> 00:36:08,329
And the gift he wants
for all his followers.

605
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:12,703
Don't you want to experience
this gift for yourself?

606
00:36:13,271 --> 00:36:15,502
I know I want you to.

607
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:18,575
Selina.

608
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:20,839
You know me.

609
00:36:21,212 --> 00:36:23,875
There isn't a single
part of Bruce Wayne's life

610
00:36:24,215 --> 00:36:25,649
that we don't know about.

611
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:29,621
His joys, his disappointments,

612
00:36:29,821 --> 00:36:32,347
his desires.

613
00:36:32,557 --> 00:36:36,551
But just like Bruce wasn't
ready to embrace his true self,

614
00:36:36,828 --> 00:36:40,287
looks like you aren't either.

615
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:43,965
Maybe.

616
00:36:44,703 --> 00:36:47,969
But one thing

617
00:36:48,306 --> 00:36:51,970
Jeremiah did teach me is I...

618
00:36:52,577 --> 00:36:54,603
(hissing): hate

619
00:36:54,846 --> 00:36:58,783
having a gun pointed at my face.

620
00:36:59,617 --> 00:37:00,617
(gunshot)

621
00:37:08,593 --> 00:37:11,654
Oh, puddin',
aren't you delicious.

622
00:37:17,669 --> 00:37:18,932
(gun clicking)

623
00:37:27,378 --> 00:37:30,246
Don't call me puddin'.

624
00:37:33,384 --> 00:37:34,977
There you go, Selina.

625
00:37:35,854 --> 00:37:37,652
I knew you had it in you.

626
00:37:38,289 --> 00:37:39,450
All it took was a little

627
00:37:39,591 --> 00:37:40,991
kick in the pants.

628
00:37:41,326 --> 00:37:42,385
Where's Jeremiah?

629
00:37:42,994 --> 00:37:44,394
Selina, drop the gun.

630
00:37:44,529 --> 00:37:47,590
Oh-oh, your boyfriend's worried.

631
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:51,027
But I still don't think
you have what it takes.

632
00:37:51,369 --> 00:37:55,602
Yeah? Well, let's see what
happens when someone deserves

633
00:37:55,740 --> 00:37:57,265
to get shot in the head.

634
00:37:57,408 --> 00:37:58,535
Selina, stop!

635
00:38:00,278 --> 00:38:01,439
(shouts)

636
00:38:07,385 --> 00:38:08,444
(shouts)

637
00:38:10,421 --> 00:38:11,514
(screams)

638
00:38:13,024 --> 00:38:13,753
Wait.

639
00:38:13,892 --> 00:38:14,892
You're bleeding.

640
00:38:14,926 --> 00:38:16,417
If you know what's good for you,

641
00:38:16,561 --> 00:38:18,962
you will let me go.

642
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:20,890
We need to get you patched up.

643
00:38:23,835 --> 00:38:24,666
What are you doing?

644
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:27,796
I have been doing it your way.

645
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:32,307
I'm gonna do it my way.

646
00:38:35,713 --> 00:38:36,806
Selina!

647
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:39,614
Selina!

648
00:38:44,355 --> 00:38:45,966
LO BOYZ LEADER: Look
at those biceps. Whoa.

649
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:47,424
I need him to build barricades.

650
00:38:47,559 --> 00:38:48,424
Nah, homie.

651
00:38:48,560 --> 00:38:50,995
This guy's got cage
match written all over him.

652
00:38:51,563 --> 00:38:53,040
I'll give you two of
mine in exchange.

653
00:38:53,064 --> 00:38:54,396
How about this.

654
00:38:56,568 --> 00:38:58,594
Drop your guns,
and I won't shoot you.

655
00:38:58,870 --> 00:39:00,014
How the hell did he get free?

656
00:39:00,038 --> 00:39:02,030
Don't matter.
He's bluffing again.

657
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:03,807
OSWALD: I'm afraid he's not.

658
00:39:04,709 --> 00:39:05,709
Neither am I.

659
00:39:07,545 --> 00:39:08,877
Come on out, boys.

660
00:39:22,060 --> 00:39:24,689
Yes, Edward, I
killed the bad men.

661
00:39:25,830 --> 00:39:27,594
Penguin shot the gang leader.

662
00:39:27,732 --> 00:39:30,930
(indistinct chatter)

663
00:39:31,069 --> 00:39:35,404
REFUGEES (chanting):
Penguin! Penguin! Penguin!

664
00:39:35,607 --> 00:39:39,544
Penguin! Penguin! Penguin!

665
00:39:39,677 --> 00:39:41,771
Penguin! Penguin!

666
00:39:41,913 --> 00:39:44,439
(chanting continues)

667
00:39:54,759 --> 00:39:56,091
You'd said we'd be safe here.

668
00:39:56,427 --> 00:39:57,907
We were better off
where we came from.

669
00:39:57,996 --> 00:39:59,692
Give it a rest, he saved us!

670
00:39:59,831 --> 00:40:01,697
(overlapping chatter)

671
00:40:01,833 --> 00:40:03,028
All right, listen up.

672
00:40:03,601 --> 00:40:04,830
- Listen to me.
- For what?

673
00:40:04,969 --> 00:40:06,437
Listen to me!

674
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,765
I know today was a hard day.

675
00:40:10,808 --> 00:40:12,572
And I can't say
there won't be others.

676
00:40:13,711 --> 00:40:14,872
But we won.

677
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:18,509
We got Penguin's
guns, his ammunition.

678
00:40:19,617 --> 00:40:20,949
We survived.

679
00:40:22,487 --> 00:40:23,682
And as long as we survive,

680
00:40:23,821 --> 00:40:26,120
hope survives in Gotham.

681
00:40:27,825 --> 00:40:29,760
I think that's
worth fighting for.

682
00:40:31,195 --> 00:40:32,663
So do I.

683
00:40:41,039 --> 00:40:42,598
There's work to be done,

684
00:40:44,842 --> 00:40:46,504
wounded to be cared for,

685
00:40:48,546 --> 00:40:50,879
food, water to be doled out.

686
00:40:52,750 --> 00:40:54,116
Tomorrow's another day.

687
00:40:54,852 --> 00:40:55,876
Go to.

688
00:41:00,158 --> 00:41:02,992
Captain, we've got
Penguin outside.

689
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:05,058
All right, give me a minute.

690
00:41:08,466 --> 00:41:09,490
Hey.

691
00:41:10,735 --> 00:41:12,601
That was a brave
thing you did there.

692
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:14,696
We wouldn't have
escaped without you.

693
00:41:15,206 --> 00:41:18,608
You saved me and my friends.

694
00:41:19,243 --> 00:41:20,575
I wanted to help.

695
00:41:21,946 --> 00:41:23,847
I can't be everywhere at once.

696
00:41:24,816 --> 00:41:27,217
I'm gonna need people I can
trust watching over this place.

697
00:41:27,986 --> 00:41:29,079
Maybe...

698
00:41:32,023 --> 00:41:34,549
you could be my
deputy here in Haven.

699
00:41:36,561 --> 00:41:37,790
WILL: Thanks.

700
00:41:37,929 --> 00:41:41,593
Because, honestly,
I'm allergic to pineapple.

701
00:41:42,033 --> 00:41:43,524
Go get 'em, Deputy.

702
00:41:51,843 --> 00:41:55,177
Jim, is this really necessary?

703
00:41:55,513 --> 00:41:58,779
I did just save, I don't
know, hundreds of people.

704
00:41:58,916 --> 00:42:01,112
After endangering
them to begin with.

705
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:03,845
Forgive me if I
wanted to play it safe.

706
00:42:03,921 --> 00:42:07,085
Still, I do hope that
there are no hard feelings.

707
00:42:07,859 --> 00:42:09,953
You did the right
thing today, Oswald.

708
00:42:10,094 --> 00:42:12,859
You're free to go, just
don't make me regret it.

709
00:42:14,165 --> 00:42:15,165
Jim!

710
00:42:16,834 --> 00:42:17,927
Harvey.

711
00:42:18,236 --> 00:42:19,727
- Hi, Pengy.
- Jim!

712
00:42:19,871 --> 00:42:21,391
- GORDON: Hold your fire.
- Bye, Pengy.

713
00:42:21,606 --> 00:42:24,075
- Barbara, no. No.
- Get out of the way! Now!

714
00:42:24,308 --> 00:42:26,834
Outside of the Green Zone,
he's fair game, but not here.

715
00:42:26,978 --> 00:42:27,775
Last chance.

716
00:42:27,912 --> 00:42:30,040
Move now or you
get my first bullet.

717
00:42:31,249 --> 00:42:32,249
I'm not moving.

718
00:43:00,111 --> 00:43:02,205
♪♪
